  "result": "The node does not pass the gate: it ends on **WITNESS_FAIL**, and both remaining failures come from the node itself, not from the Lean. Every other witness passes (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_2, branch_3, branch_4), plus the five I added (branch_6 to branch_10: emergency vehicle, police officer, red signal, stop sign, and an overlong halt at the mail drop box).\n\n**The two failures:**\n\n1. **branch_1 cannot be not_applicable.** This run's reading lists no included class for the tour bus, shuttle bus, limo or RTC bus aggregates; every vehicle class is \"unresolved\". Core only counts a road user as a member when it carries an included class, so exceptions (2) and (3) can never hold. The tour bus scene therefore comes out unknown. To fix it, either the reading includes at least one class in those aggregates (e.g. `ru.tour_bus_or_limousine`), or branch_1 is re-planned to expect unknown.\n2. **branch_5 contradicts the node's own obligation.** The node puts \"halted behind traffic in the lane\" inside the obligation (halt implies queue or a directed halt). A queued halt is therefore compliant, but the plan expects not_applicable. I wrote the obligation as the record states it. To fix it, either branch_5 expects compliant, or the queue and directed-halt exclusions move into the applicability. In that case my device witnesses (branch_7 to branch_9) would need to expect not_applicable too.\n\n**One choice I made:** in exceptions (2), (3) and (5), the time-since-halting test also requires the vehicle to be at rest now. This only turns not_applicable into compliant while the vehicle is moving, so it never changes the duty. I explained it in the rule's header rather than declaring a narrowing, because those spans are exceptions and must not be narrowed.\n\n**Gate runs:** I used 5 of the 6. Three were wasted: one on the unmodified skeleton and two started by accident. One real fix went in: the mail drop box needed an outline. The last run is unused, since only a change to the node can fix what's left.\n\nFiles are in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/LVMC_11_52_030_A/`:\n- task_result.md",
